If you have updated some Access keys or secret keys in README file and want to push to Github , it will throw an error and prevents from pushing to Github because of security reasons. So you have to remove those keys from README file and then push to Github.
Even if you remove those keys from README file and push to Github, those keys are still there in the commit history. So you have to remove those keys from commit history as well using below command - 
git filter-branch --force --index-filter 
git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch README.md --prune-empty --tag-name-filter cat -- --all


git reset --hard HEAD~1  # This will remove the last one commit and all the changes in that commit will be lost, so be careful while using this command.



######################## Increase Disk Space of LVM ##################################
sudo lsblk # to check the disk space
sudo fdisk /dev/xvda  # to create a new partition on the disk
sudo partprobe  # to update the kernel about the new partition
sudo pvcreate /dev/xvda3  # to create a physical volume on the new partition
sudo vgextend VolGroup00 /dev/xvda3  # to extend the volume group
sudo lvextend -l +100%FREE /dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00  # to extend the logical volume
sudo lvextend -r -L +5G /dev/mapper/RootVG-homeVolume  # to extend the logical volume and resize the filesystem
sudo resize2fs /dev/VolGroup00/LogVol00  # to resize the
sudo growpart /dev/nvme0n1 4 # to grow the partition 4 is the partition number which we want to grow

